WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.035
-You know, New York, y'all ain't
playing around.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.137
I just had to make sure.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.305
-No, yeah, we're good.
No, we're good.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.773
-Y'all are not playing around
out here.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.741
-We don't play around in NBC.
-But I'm happy to be outside.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.443
-Yeah, exactly.
-See everybody.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.412
-Look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.613
-Come on!
-Look at that.

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.115
Come on.

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:18.751
-You can see the bottom of
people's faces now.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.886
-Yes.
-Taking the mask off.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.489
-Yeah, you can see, yeah.
-'Cause that tripped me out.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.957
I was working on this movie,
and, you know,

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.725
everybody's eyes look beautiful.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:29.395
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.597
I was talking to this girl
for like six months,

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:32.731
but all I saw was this.

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:34.667
She took that thing off,
I was like, "Okay!"

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.902
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:38.771
The bottom of the face
looks different, right?

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.874
I was like, "Oh, man!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.843
[ Hisses ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.244
"Put the mask back on." Yeah.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.280
-She's like, "We going out?"
I'm like, "Yeah, I'm going."

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.781
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.216
-One of us is going out,
absolutely.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.652
-This COVID is crazy, man,
especially being black, too.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.887
It's crazy.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.354
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.524
No, I'm just saying because I
knew it was going to be tough

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.492
for brothers during COVID just
the way we greet each other.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:03.295
Like, when I saw you,
I was like, "Oh!"

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:04.998
[ Coughs ]

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:09.368
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.404
-Yeah, no, no, no.
We elbowed each other.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.372
-Yeah, you right,
you right, you right.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.006
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:17.409
My white friend.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.245
-Should we talk about the book?

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.514
-Oh, yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.283
-You have a giant book
coming out Tuesday.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.186
"Act Like You Got Some Sense:

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.221
And Other Things
I Taught My Daughters,"

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.456
crossed it out and put
"My Daughters Taught Me."

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.725
-Yeah.
-"Act Like You Got Some Sense."

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.327
That came from your grandma?
-That came from my grandmother.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:40.533
When I won the Oscar for "Ray,"
in my speech,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.135
I thanked my grandmother,
because I said

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.871
she's the first person
who was my acting teacher.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.772
She told me,
"Act like you got some sense."

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:49.475
You know, it's culture,
but, like, when you're black

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.443
and you're going into a grocery
store, your mother says,

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:52.912
"Now, you act like you got
some sense in here.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.414
Don't you pick up nothing,
because you might,

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.915
you know, lose a limb
or whatever."

00:01:55.915 --> 00:02:01.921
So I used that title because I
used sort of the disciplines of

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.891
what my grandmother and
grandfather taught me in Texas

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:09.595
to try to apply with my
two young girls in Hollywood,

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.964
which in the book, you see
it doesn't always work.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.133
But that's where that came from.
-No, I think that's what I took

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.969
from the book,
and what I love about the book

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.738
is I think that you started
a communication with your kids

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.274
that you don't talk to them
like kids.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.476
You talk to them like --
I mean, you're an adult

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.812
and you're the dad,
but you go, "Let's talk."

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.080
-Because of what I think --

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.614
You know, it's not
a big message book

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.015
'cause it's a lot of funny stuff
in it,

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:31.851
but what I was always trying to
make people understand,

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.520
I wanted to break down those
barriers with your daughters

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.256
because your daughters
are going to need you,

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.158
especially when it comes to,
like, guys and relationships.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:42.060
I mean, who else would
know better than us?

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.230
And so by doing it early,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.200
which a lot of people frowned at
first, but now it pays dividends

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.634
when they really have
serious questions

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.369
about guys
that I'm going to kill.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:57.343
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:01.814
-Can you tell the story about
how you had -- you enlisted

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.516
Snoop Dogg to help intimidate
your daughter's boyfriend?

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:06.585
-What happened was my daughter,

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.755
who didn't know that I had
already run a background check

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:13.292
on her boyfriend,
he comes to the crib,

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:14.960
and Snoop happens to be there.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.862
And I said, "Snoop, there he is
right there."

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.731
[ Laughter ]
"Shake him up."

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:22.067
And you know Snoop, you know,
Snoop walked over to

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:25.071
my daughter's boyfriend
and just said, "Hey, what's up?

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:28.541
What's up, cuz? You know?
Hey, look here. You know.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.444
We her uncles,
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.913
So act accordingly, homey."

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.949
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:42.088
But the underlying meaning of it
was is that I wanted

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.522
the young man to understand

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:46.158
that she's got people
that really love her.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:50.029
So that if something does
go wrong, Snoop is coming to...

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.697
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, no.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:55.134
Your book tour...
[ Applause ]

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.137
Your book tour kicks off
Friday night in Philly.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.372
Then on Saturday night
you're in Harlem.

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:02.808
-Friday night in Philly!
-Roots.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.745
-Friday night in Philly!

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.246
Friday night in Philly!

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.481
-Whoo!

